% inspect_let_scope.trx -- PTY gate for github issue #14 (S12).
% The inspector halts inside a `[/name] let` scope.  That scope dict is
% sized to exactly its bound names, so while it was a FIXED dict the
% debugger's own `def` -- it runs Trix code in the interrupted program's
% dict context -- overflowed it, and the session died before drawing a
% single frame.  Keep this file free of the error name the scenario
% greps for as a FORBIDDEN marker: the source pane renders these very
% comments into the capture.  The feeder's q ends the session.
/log-msg { [/msg] let msg = end } def

(inside-let) log-msg
(after-let) =
